{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/717852-hunting-tips","id":717852,"title":"Hunting tips","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-23T00:28:01-07:00","id":717852,"title":"Hunting tips","content":"Hi guys<br /> my troupe want to build up an Iron Master pack. Two rahu, two elodoth (one a blood talon), an Ithaeur, one irraka and a cahalith (hunter in darkness).<br /> They will be character with 25/30 exp.<br /> They ask me if they can hunt mages as primary prey. We will probably start the chronicle when MtA2 is out.<br /> Do you have any tips to hunt such a prey?<br /> <br /> Please, I don't want to create a vs thread.<br /> Not a werewolf vs mage thread, just how to <b><i>find and kill mages.</i></b> I'm not interested in 1 vs 1 or honorable fight, just do what uratha do: hunt and kill.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T00:50:52-07:00","id":717991,"title":"","content":"Too many variables to offer meaningful advice that is not equally applicable to any other unknown quantity. What sort of mages do you intend to present as potential targets?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T00:55:38-07:00","id":718024,"title":"","content":"They surprise mages! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Mages are most dangerous when prepared - especially in 2ED they will be, with Supernal Magic rules centered on rituals and making spontaneous casting creating Paradoxes.<br /> <br /> Iron Masters shtick is blending in with the crowd and so should the pack. Hishu Form now let you seem as totally human to supernaturals, so use it. Hide in the crowd, sneak past mages, and kill them when they think you are simple human. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T01:15:22-07:00","id":718063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/717852-hunting-tips?p=717991#post717991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too many variables to offer meaningful advice that is not equally applicable to any other unknown quantity. What sort of mages do you intend to present as potential targets?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably mixed paths. But probably from Mysterium and Guardians of the Veil. I think I'll go with a cabal made up to find and hold powerful Loci<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They surprise mages! <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> Mages are most dangerous when prepared - especially in 2ED they will be, with Supernal Magic rules centered on rituals and making spontaneous casting creating Paradoxes.<br /> <br /> Iron Masters shtick is blending in with the crowd and so should the pack. Hishu Form now let you seem as totally human to supernaturals, so use it. Hide in the crowd, sneak past mages, and kill them when they think you are simple human. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I was thinking about it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But with some spells I think is quite possible to find an uratha even in hishu, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 10-23-2015, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T01:50:09-07:00","id":718149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/717852-hunting-tips?p=718063#post718063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, I was thinking about it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But with some spells I think is quite possible to find an uratha even in hishu, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>How I understand the rules, no supernatural can even feel that Hishu form is more than the &quot;Sleeper&quot; until observer uses somekind of the powers. Active Mage Sight will probably be enough - but until mage cast it, werewolf in Hishu is perfectly ordinary &quot;Sleeper&quot; to them. Just kill your target before he look on you face. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Or just send on them Spirits Assasins. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-23-2015, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T02:51:04-07:00","id":718367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/717852-hunting-tips?p=718063#post718063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, I was thinking about it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But with some spells I think is quite possible to find an uratha even in hishu, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would still be penalized by PU. I'd make an easy fetish to double that penalty. if I was hunting mages.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T02:53:05-07:00","id":718371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/717852-hunting-tips?p=718149#post718149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How I understand the rules, no supernatural can even feel that Hishu form is more than the &quot;Sleeper&quot; until observer uses somekind of the powers. Active Mage Sight will probably be enough - but until mage cast it, werewolf in Hishu is perfectly ordinary &quot;Sleeper&quot; to them. Just kill your target before he look on you face. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Resonance work in layers. The Hishu disguise is the first layer of defense. Just turning on mage sight doesn't works, the mage has to look specifically at the normal-looking Uratha, which is successful scrutiny.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T04:55:36-07:00","id":718644,"title":"","content":"You're gonna want plenty of Feet of Mist and Ward the Wolf's Den to help counter scrying, divinations, portals etc when the sorcerers start to try and pin down who is responsible for the hunts and counterattack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T05:06:04-07:00","id":718653,"title":"","content":"Well of course they can do it.<br /> <br /> At least one of them should have Scent the Unnatural or Lore of the Land, and you might give them access to a fetish like Hexesucher from Night Horrors: the Unbidden or a totem associated with witch hunting, like the spirit from Hexesucher. Something to provide the characters with or supplement their reason for focusing on mages.<br /> <br /> You also might want to give the Mages some plots and motives of their own that will give the werewolves some reason to hunt them other than them just being magic users. Grabbing loci might do it but you might want more. And if they don't have the abilities that let them sense out mages, whatever the mages are doing should be something that would allow the werewolves to notice them doing magic, unless you want to play up the, 'they can be anyone' angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-23-2015, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T07:05:21-07:00","id":718892,"title":"","content":"Mages specialize in information gathering and shields. You want to hit them when they're unprepared, so lean heavily on the Irraka's tactics. Surprise is your best option, hit hard, hit fast. Gather all your information without them learning about you. If they're in the know, then try to come up with an out-of-the-box tactic, like just hitting them with a bus instead of a direct attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T07:07:49-07:00","id":718898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/717852-hunting-tips?p=718063#post718063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, I was thinking about it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But with some spells I think is quite possible to find an uratha even in hishu, right?</div> </div> </div> </div> Those would be sympathetic magic, which requires a connection, and often the name of the target. So, don't leave behind blood or hair, don't let them know your name, and you hsould be fine.<br /> <br /> If you mean spotting someone with Mage Sight? That tends to require actually -looking- at each individual. If they don't see you coming, they won't know to look, and they won't know. Information is a mage's strength, but insufficent information is their bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-23-2015, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T07:49:52-07:00","id":719166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/717852-hunting-tips?p=718653#post718653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well of course they can do it.<br /> <br /> At least one of them should have Scent the Unnatural or Lore of the Land, and you might give them access to a fetish like Hexesucher from Night Horrors: the Unbidden or a totem associated with witch hunting, like the spirit from Hexesucher. Something to provide the characters with or supplement their reason for focusing on mages.<br /> <br /> You also might want to give the Mages some plots and motives of their own that will give the werewolves some reason to hunt them other than them just being magic users. Grabbing loci might do it but you might want more. And if they don't have the abilities that let them sense out mages, whatever the mages are doing should be something that would allow the werewolves to notice them doing magic, unless you want to play up the, 'they can be anyone' angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course you're right but I was just asking myself about hunting mages, I have already a couple of Idea about a cabal of Mysterium and Guardians who finds and take an ancient-lost urban Locus.<br /> But I'll think about it. My thread is not only to understand some dinamycs but also for curiosity<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages specialize in information gathering and shields. You want to hit them when they're unprepared, so lean heavily on the Irraka's tactics </div> </div> </div>- Gaining Informations with irraka tactics and Ithaur tactics, hishu form could be a good idea<br /> - Let the elodoth do his job with his allies and contacts starting the siskur da<br /> - Targeting the leader with the cahalith gift can be a good idea<br /> - Striking with Irraka first, rahu after trying to smash them after some irraka-urshul work, an iron master-like tactic with fetishes and other weapons<br /> boosted with shaping and tech gifts. Ithaeur and elodoth support could be great with spirits ecc.<br /> - Be prepared for some kind of counterattack<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T08:00:34-07:00","id":719204,"title":"","content":"Feet of Mist helps considerably with the &quot;leave no trace!&quot; part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}